`IDENTITY-LOCK-MISMATCH`, `COLLECTION-LOG-DIGEST`, `COLLECTION-LOG-NOT-IN-WITNESS-COMMIT`). Fixtures: `test_build_corpus_identity_v19.py` `fba963557b8fb961b15b0eebf627460fd8b1cf70d1a248bd70c76a1fe81d046b` (5 tests: accepted-witnessed-locked with the history; every attempt logged including RETRY and witness refusals; a conflicting later ACCEPT logged and locked out; adoption must be a blob at the approval commit; identity carries lock/T_pulse/adoption); `test_run_configurations_v3.py` `642805b2b47a8d45017db3077cac5ec9c303425fb9c3490a5b8c8ca45f8902d1` (20 tests: V15's 17, plus adoption-fails-closed, sentinel-counted-and-unscored, and the acceptance-path refusals; its end-to-end test drives the V19 builder over a real git scaffold into the driver). COST: (i) the NIST primary is, in practice, given up — under V15 the fallback could not open before T_pulse + 24 h, so NIST had at least that long to serve a verifying certificate and was checked live at each later build; under V17 NIST is tried live at build time, at or after T_pulse, once, so the seed will almost certainly come from drand, whose BLS proof this lane cannot verify (LIMIT (ii)); the seed's provenance therefore rests on agreement of ≥ 2 of 4 pinned relays, retained and live, not on a signature verified to a pinned root — a weaker provenance, accepted with eyes open; (ii) the V15 signature and its RETRY record become history: one signed commitment whose seed was never drawn, on file forever, and the register will show a V15 signed-then-superseded row; (iii) nothing else — no sample size, floor, bar, exclusion, attempt count, custody or protection rule moves. PRESERVED: V15's bytes and digest, its signature record, the RETRY beacon record, every pin V15 carries except the three files named above. ORDER: the server-side push event (W3) and the nonce (W5) of step (1a) bound the approval record on both sides; MIN_T_SIGN and EXCLUDED_T_PULSE are lower bounds only; the change record carries the timeline (finding 11:0